{'symbol': 'ZBRA', 'date': '2020-02-13 09:30:00', 'title': 'ZEBRA TECHNOLOGIES ANNOUNCES Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.10', 'text': "ZEBRA TECHNOLOGIES ANNOUNCES FOURTH-QUARTER AND FULL-YEAR 2019 RESULTS.Q4 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.56.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.10.Q4 SALES $1.192 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.2 BILLION.SEES Q1 2020 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.90 TO $3.10.SEES FY 2020 SALES UP ABOUT 4 TO 6 PERCENT.SEES Q1 2020 SALES UP ABOUT 4 TO 7 PERCENT.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $3.65 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ISSUES OUTLOOK FOR Q1 AND FULL YEAR 2020 WITHOUT TAKING INTO ACCOUNT FULL POTENTIAL IMPACT OF CORONAVIRUS OUTBREAK IN CHINA.COMPANY EXPECTS FIRST-QUARTER 2020 NET SALES TO INCREASE APPROXIMATELY 4% TO 7% FROM Q1 OF 2019.ADJUSTED EBITDA MARGIN IS EXPECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY 20% FOR Q1 OF 2020.FOR FULL-YEAR 2020, COMPANY EXPECTS TO GENERATE FREE CASH FLOW OF AT LEAST $700 MILLION.CURRENT EXPECTATION IS CORONAVIRUS OUTBREAK COULD HAVE AN IMPACT ON SALES OF BETWEEN $0 AND $50 MILLION.ZEBRA TECHNOLOGIES - NOT YET ABLE TO FULLY ASCERTAIN POTENTIAL IMPACT OF CORONAVIRUS OUTBREAK ON RESULTS OF OPERATIONS, CO'S MANUFACTURING IN CHINA."}